  { number := 97, text := "## 3. Definitions" },
  { number := 98, text := "" },
  { number := 99, text := "### 3.1 Copyright held" },
  { number := 100, text := "" },
  { number := 101, text := "The status in which a work still has a copyright holder. A later contract can still take that work because the holder, or a successor, can still grant, sell, or wrap the work in private terms." },
  { number := 102, text := "" },
  { number := 103, text := "### 3.2 Public domain dedication" },
  { number := 104, text := "" },
  { number := 105, text := "The status in which the author dedicated copyright interest in the work to the public domain, as an overt act of relinquishment, so the work stays the common heritage of anyone who seeks it, outside a later private claim by that author or by that author's heirs." },
  { number := 106, text := "" },
  { number := 107, text := "### 3.3 Grant that keeps copyright" },
  { number := 108, text := "" },
  { number := 109, text := "A grant that lets others use, copy, or change a work while the author still holds copyright. Such a grant is not a public domain dedication. Remaining copyright still lets a later contract take the work. MIT and Apache 2.0 are grants that keep copyright." },
  { number := 110, text := "" },
  { number := 111, text := "### 3.4 Public Domain Open Source Software" },
  { number := 112, text := "" },
  { number := 113, text := "Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is the ideal: software dedicated to the public domain that remains open (source available; use, copy, modify, and distribute without a grant that keeps copyright). PDOSS is this specification. Unlicense remains the license that this repository uses to meet PDOSS." },
  { number := 114, text := "" },
  { number := 115, text := "### 3.5 PDOSS test" },
  { number := 116, text := "" },
  { number := 117, text := "The PDOSS test is the named test of this specification. A dedication meets the PDOSS test if and only if it is a public domain dedication of software that is open (source available; use, copy, modify, and distribute without a grant that keeps copyright). A license that keeps copyright is not a public domain dedication and does not meet the PDOSS test. Companion Lean encodes that test as `meetsPdoss`." },
  { number := 118, text := "" },
  { number := 119, text := "### 3.6 Unlicense" },
  { number := 120, text := "" },
  { number := 121, text := "The public domain dedication recorded in `UNLICENSE.md`. In jurisdictions that recognize copyright, the author dedicated copyright interest in the covered work to the public domain. The Unlicense is not a grant that keeps copyright. The Unlicense is not a claim that every file on disk in this clone is covered (Clause 4.5 names residual licenses). Unlicense remains the license. The Unlicense meets the PDOSS test." },
  { number := 122, text := "" },
