  { number := 168, text := "" },
  { number := 169, text := "The Allow list is the list of jurisdictions whose statute lets an Author waive the moral right of attribution for software, or carves software out of that right. Nationals of those jurisdictions MAY contribute if they dedicate the Contribution under the Unlicense." },
  { number := 170, text := "" },
  { number := 171, text := "### 3.19 Specific consent list" },
  { number := 172, text := "" },
  { number := 173, text := "The Specific consent list is the list of jurisdictions whose statute requires consent that identifies the Work and the uses. A blanket Unlicense is not that consent." },
  { number := 174, text := "" },
  { number := 175, text := "### 3.20 Residual attribution list" },
  { number := 176, text := "" },
  { number := 177, text := "The Residual attribution list is the list of jurisdictions whose statute keeps the moral right of attribution after a public domain dedication or after assignment of copyright." },
  { number := 178, text := "" },
  { number := 179, text := "### 3.21 Unread list" },
  { number := 180, text := "" },
  { number := 181, text := "The Unread list is the list of jurisdictions whose copyright statute has not been classified into Allow, Specific consent, or Residual attribution in this specification. Unread is not a finding that attribution cannot be waived. Unread is not a finding that attribution can be waived. Unread is refusal until classification." },
  { number := 182, text := "" },
  { number := 183, text := "### 3.22 Moral right of attribution" },
  { number := 184, text := "" },
  { number := 185, text := "The moral right of attribution is the Author's right to be identified as the Author of the Work, also called the right of paternity, or droit de paternite (French moral right of authorship). It is distinct from economic copyright. It is distinct from the moral right of integrity." },
  { number := 186, text := "" },
  { number := 187, text := "### 3.23 Waiver" },
  { number := 188, text := "" },
  { number := 189, text := "A Waiver is a written act by which the Author gives up the power to enforce a right, including the moral right of attribution." },
  { number := 190, text := "" },
  { number := 191, text := "### 3.24 Assignment" },
  { number := 192, text := "" },
  { number := 193, text := "An Assignment is a transfer of a right to another person. A right that cannot be assigned may still be waivable, or it may not. Those are different operations." },
