  { number := 195, text := "## 4. Core requirements" },
  { number := 196, text := "" },
  { number := 197, text := "### 4.1 A grant that keeps copyright still lets a later contract take the work" },
  { number := 198, text := "" },
  { number := 199, text := "1. A grant that keeps copyright (Clause 3.3) SHALL be treated as still leaving a copyright holder." },
  { number := 200, text := "2. Remaining copyright SHALL be treated as still letting a later contract take the work." },
  { number := 201, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT treat a grant that keeps copyright as if it were a public domain dedication." },
  { number := 202, text := "4. Companion Lean SHALL encode remaining copyright on a grant that keeps copyright and has no dedication (`ossWithoutDedication`). This document does not paste that encoding." },
  { number := 203, text := "" },
  { number := 204, text := "### 4.2 The PDOSS test and Unlicense" },
  { number := 205, text := "" },
  { number := 206, text := "1. Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) SHALL be treated as the ideal." },
  { number := 207, text := "2. A dedication SHALL meet the PDOSS test (Clause 3.5) if and only if it is a public domain dedication of software that is open (source available; use, copy, modify, and distribute without a grant that keeps copyright)." },
  { number := 208, text := "3. Unlicense remains the license. The most important Surmount work in this repository (Clause 3.12) SHALL be dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense so it stays the common heritage of anyone who seeks it, outside a later private claim." },
  { number := 209, text := "4. The Unlicense SHALL be treated as a public domain dedication (Clause 3.2 and Clause 3.6), not as a grant that keeps copyright." },
  { number := 210, text := "5. Companion Lean SHALL encode that an Unlicense dedication has no remaining copyright in the model (`unlicenseDedication`) and that Unlicense meets the PDOSS test (`meetsPdoss`). This document does not paste those encodings." },
  { number := 211, text := "6. Anyone is free to copy, modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute covered work, either in source form or as a compiled binary, for any purpose, commercial or noncommercial, and by any means, as `UNLICENSE.md` records." },
  { number := 212, text := "" },
  { number := 213, text := "### 4.3 MIT and Apache 2.0 do not meet a public domain dedication test" },
  { number := 214, text := "" },
  { number := 215, text := "1. MIT as used by the Lean 4 agent skill pack at `skills/lean4-skills` SHALL be treated as a grant that keeps copyright. MIT SHALL NOT meet a public domain dedication test. MIT SHALL NOT meet the PDOSS test." },
  { number := 216, text := "2. Apache 2.0 as used by the `btc-verified` pin at `ref/btc-verified` SHALL be treated as a grant that keeps copyright. Apache 2.0 SHALL NOT meet a public domain dedication test. Apache 2.0 SHALL NOT meet the PDOSS test." },
  { number := 217, text := "3. Companion Lean SHALL encode MIT and Apache 2.0 as distinct constructors (`mitGrant` and `apacheTwo`). Companion Lean SHALL prove those constructors do not meet the PDOSS test. This document does not paste those proofs." },
  { number := 218, text := "4. A mash that claims MIT meets PDOSS (`mitMeetsPdoss`) SHALL be treated as `False`. Companion Lean SHALL prove `mash_mit_meets_pdoss`. This document does not paste that theorem." },
  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "### 4.4 Ideas are not scarce" },
  { number := 221, text := "" },
  { number := 222, text := "1. Ideas SHALL be treated as not scarce." },
  { number := 223, text := "2. Two people SHALL be treated as able to hold the same idea at once." },
  { number := 224, text := "3. Generosity of ideas SHALL be the default this repository chooses." },
  { number := 225, text := "4. Companion Lean SHALL encode `ideasNonScarce` and `ideasNotRivalrous`. This document does not paste those encodings." },
  { number := 226, text := "" },
  { number := 227, text := "### 4.5 This repository Unlicense except named residual licenses" },
  { number := 228, text := "" },
  { number := 229, text := "1. Authors in this repository SHALL release numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license." },
  { number := 230, text := "2. The Lean 4 agent skill pack at `skills/lean4-skills` remains original work under the MIT license. This repository's Unlicense SHALL NOT be read as replacing that MIT license." },
  { number := 231, text := "3. Essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense grants. This repository's Unlicense SHALL NOT be read as applying the Unlicense to those essays." },
  { number := 232, text := "4. The `btc-verified` pin at `ref/btc-verified` remains Apache 2.0. This repository's Unlicense SHALL NOT be read as replacing that Apache 2.0 license." },
  { number := 233, text := "5. Companion Lean SHALL encode `thisRepoUnlicenseExceptNamedResidual`. This document does not paste that encoding." },
  { number := 234, text := "" },
  { number := 235, text := "### 4.6 Refuse a tool the author cannot improve" },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "1. A person who builds tools SHALL refuse a tool they cannot improve." },
  { number := 238, text := "2. That requirement is process residual under `0006_RSI.md`. It is not a claim that every product is Unlicense." },
  { number := 239, text := "3. Companion Lean SHALL encode that refusing a tool the author cannot improve is RSI process and is not a license claim on every product. This document does not paste that encoding." },
  { number := 240, text := "" },
  { number := 241, text := "### 4.7 Formal Vibefication split" },
  { number := 242, text := "" },
  { number := 243, text := "1. Numbered markdown in this specifications repository is the contract humans read. The specification SHALL also be encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true. Proofs SHALL live in separate Lean modules. Lean proofs are not the specification. Numbered markdown is not a substitute for those encodings. They SHALL stay separate in this repository as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`." },
  { number := 244, text := "2. For this specification the spec encoding module is `lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean`. The proof module is `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean`. Lake keeps those library names. The product name of this specification is PDOSS." },
  { number := 245, text := "3. Mixing spec encoding declarations and their proofs in one mash that hides the split (Clause 3.9) is nonconforming for this specifications repository." },
  { number := 246, text := "4. Companion Lean SHALL treat a mash of spec encoding and proof as `False` (see `mash_spec_and_proof`). This document does not paste that theorem." },
  { number := 247, text := "5. Every published numbered specification markdown `NNNN_descriptive_name.md` at this repository root SHALL have an adjacent Lean spec encoding `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` at the same root (Clause 3.11). Proofs of those encodings SHALL live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, not in `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean`." },
  { number := 248, text := "6. `lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean` remains the meaning encoding of this specification. `0009_PDOSS.lean` is the line encoding of this markdown file. Those are not the same module." },
  { number := 249, text := "" },
  { number := 250, text := "### 4.8 Back linking and exact theorems" },
  { number := 251, text := "" },
  { number := 252, text := "1. Citations of Formal Vibefication SHALL include the canonical URL https://proofofkeags.com/research/2026-05-12-formal-vibefication.html ." },
  { number := 253, text := "2. A numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags MUST also contain the host `proofofkeags.com`." },
  { number := 254, text := "3. Theorems cover exactly what they state. Dedication of this repository is not a proof that essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are public domain. Dedication of this repository is not a proof that the Lean 4 agent skill pack is Unlicense. Dedication of this repository is not a proof that the `btc-verified` pin is Unlicense." },
  { number := 255, text := "4. On 2026-08-25, Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) was asked which jurisdiction applies. He answered USA. He said back linking is ideal. This is not an Unlicense grant of those essays." },
  { number := 256, text := "" },
  { number := 257, text := "### 4.9 Product honesty" },
  { number := 258, text := "" },
  { number := 259, text := "1. beastdb work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that beastdb never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 260, text := "2. SSSSS work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that SSSSS never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 261, text := "3. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Slake never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 262, text := "4. Continuous Integration work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Continuous Integration never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 263, text := "5. Lean Machine work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Lean Machine never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 264, text := "6. Majestic Memex work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Authors MUST NOT write that Majestic Memex never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 265, text := "7. This specification does not claim a conforming PDOSS product exists beyond the dedication, encodings, and proofs named here." },
  { number := 266, text := "" },
  { number := 267, text := "### 4.10 Unassigned numbers and unspecified products" },
  { number := 268, text := "" },
  { number := 269, text := "1. fargo is unspecified. fargo has no numbered specification and no assigned number. Authors SHALL NOT invent a numbered specification file for fargo in this effort." },
  { number := 270, text := "2. SSSP is unspecified. SSSP has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 271, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is unspecified. Carbonado has no numbered specification file and no assigned number." },
  { number := 272, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 273, text := "5. Number 0009 is this specification. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Authors SHALL NOT assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. Mentions of Vocabulary as a published specification 0009 do not conform." },
  { number := 274, text := "6. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. The Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 275, text := "" },
  { number := 276, text := "### 4.11 Named gate" },
  { number := 277, text := "" },
  { number := 278, text := "1. The named gate for this specifications repository remains the gate specified in `0007_CI.md`:" },
  { number := 279, text := "" },
  { number := 280, text := "```text" },
  { number := 281, text := "nix flake check \"path:$PWD\" --print-build-logs" },
  { number := 282, text := "```" },
  { number := 283, text := "" },
  { number := 284, text := "2. Lean 4 SHALL be used to surface logical inconsistency in the encodings and in the proofs." },
