  { number := 286, text := "### 4.12 Contributor nationality condition" },
  { number := 287, text := "" },
  { number := 288, text := "This clause is the contributor facing text of this specification. It does not change the Unlicense text applied to published Works. The Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 MUST NOT exist. The license text of each Work remains `UNLICENSE.md`." },
  { number := 289, text := "" },
  { number := 290, text := "1. A User of a published Work MAY run, copy, study, modify, and distribute that Work under the Unlicense. No permission, payment, or authorship credit is required. Nationality SHALL NOT restrict use of a published Work. Companion Lean encodes `usersRestrictedByNationality` as false." },
  { number := 291, text := "2. A Contribution is a different act. A Contribution SHALL be accepted only if both of the following hold:" },
  { number := 292, text := "	1. the Contributor dedicates it under the Unlicense; and" },
  { number := 293, text := "	2. every nationality the Contributor holds is on the Allow list (Clause 3.18 and Clause 4.13)." },
  { number := 294, text := "3. A Contribution SHALL be refused if the Contributor holds any nationality on the Residual attribution list, the Specific consent list, or the Unread list." },
  { number := 295, text := "4. If any one citizenship is on the Residual attribution list, the Specific consent list, or the Unread list, the Contribution SHALL be refused. Dual or multiple nationality is that any not Allow class, not a separate license." },
  { number := 296, text := "5. Residence, visa, employer, and server location SHALL NOT change the condition. Nationality is citizenship (Clause 3.17). Companion Lean encodes `nationalityIsCitizenship`." },
  { number := 297, text := "6. Companion Lean SHALL encode `NationalityClass` as Allow, specific consent, residual attribution, and unread, SHALL encode a `Contribution` as Unlicense dedication plus a list of those classes, and SHALL treat `contributionAccepted` as true if and only if the Contribution is dedicated under the Unlicense and every nationality class is Allow. Companion Lean SHALL prove `mash_residual_attribution_contribution_accepted` as `False`. This document does not paste those encodings." },
  { number := 298, text := "7. Surmount Systems SHALL refuse inbound licenses other than the Unlicense. MIT, Apache 2.0, and GPL are grants that keep copyright. A grant that keeps copyright SHALL NOT meet the PDOSS test (Clause 4.3). The nationality filter is a separate rule because, in some jurisdictions, a moral right of attribution can survive a dedication." },
  { number := 299, text := "8. This specification does not require government identity documents, a copyright office filing, or proof of citizenship from a state. The Contributor attests nationality. A false attestation SHALL be treated as a refused Contribution." },
  { number := 300, text := "" },
  { number := 301, text := "### 4.13 Allow list" },
