  { number := 369, text := "Nationals of these jurisdictions SHALL NOT contribute. After a public domain dedication, the statute still lets the Author enforce the moral right of attribution." },
  { number := 370, text := "" },
  { number := 371, text := "#### 4.15.1 Unwaivable or inalienable attribution" },
  { number := 372, text := "" },
  { number := 373, text := "The statute states that the moral right of attribution cannot be waived, that a waiver is void, that the right is inalienable or cannot be given up, or that a waiver is valid only for a use limited in kind and extent (which a worldwide perpetual dedication is not)." },
