  { number := 409, text := "35. Japan. `Copyright Act` Art. 59. Exclusively personal and inalienable." },
  { number := 410, text := "36. Kazakhstan. `Law 6-I` Art. 15(4). Personal non property rights are inalienable." },
  { number := 411, text := "37. Macao. `Decree-Law 43/99/M` Arts. 7(d) and 41. Perpetual, inalienable, cannot be given up, cannot expire by time. Not a United Nations member." },
  { number := 412, text := "38. Mali. `Bangui Agreement Annex VII` Art. 7(4)." },
  { number := 413, text := "39. Mauritania. `Bangui Agreement Annex VII` Art. 7(4)." },
  { number := 414, text := "40. Mexico. `Ley Federal del Derecho de Autor` Arts. 19 and 21. Inalienable, cannot expire by time, cannot be waived, cannot be seized, including recognition as Author." },
  { number := 415, text := "41. Republic of Moldova. `Law on Copyright` Art. 9. Inalienable." },
  { number := 416, text := "42. Niger. `Bangui Agreement Annex VII` Art. 7(4)." },
  { number := 417, text := "43. Norway. `Andsverkloven` section 5 (Norwegian Copyright Act). Waiver only for a use limited in character and extent." },
  { number := 418, text := "44. Oman. `Royal Decree 65/2008` Art. 5. Perpetual, inalienable, cannot be assigned." },
  { number := 419, text := "45. Peru. `Andean Community Decision 351` Art. 11." },
  { number := 420, text := "46. Poland. `Act on Copyright and Related Rights 1994` Art. 16. Unlimited in time; not subject to waiver or transfer; includes authorship and naming." },
  { number := 421, text := "47. Portugal. `Codigo do Direito de Autor e dos Direitos Conexos` Art. 56 (Portuguese Copyright Code). Inalienable, cannot be waived, cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 422, text := "48. Romania. `Law 8/1996` Arts. 10 and 11(1). May not be waived or transferred." },
  { number := 423, text := "49. Russian Federation. `Civil Code` Art. 1265. Authorship and the right to a name are inalienable; a waiver is void." },
  { number := 424, text := "50. Saudi Arabia. Copyright Law published 13 February 2026 in `Umm Al Qura`. Moral rights perpetual, cannot be transferred, cannot be waived." },
  { number := 425, text := "51. Senegal. `Bangui Agreement Annex VII` Art. 7(4)." },
  { number := 426, text := "52. Slovakia. `Copyright Act` Art. 17(2). The Author may not waive; cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 427, text := "53. Spain. `Ley de Propiedad Intelectual` Art. 14. Cannot be waived and inalienable, including recognition as Author." },
  { number := 428, text := "54. Sweden. `Upphovsrattsslagen 1960:729` 3 section (Swedish Copyright Act). Waiver only for a use limited as to character and scope." },
  { number := 429, text := "55. Togo. `Bangui Agreement Annex VII` Art. 7(4)." },
  { number := 430, text := "56. Turkey. `Law 5846` Arts. 14 to 16. Inalienable; contractual waiver of honor protection is void." },
  { number := 431, text := "57. United Arab Emirates. `Federal Decree-Law 38 of 2021` Art. 5. Moral rights are not subject to prescription or assignment; commentary treats them as not waivable." },
  { number := 432, text := "58. Viet Nam. `Law on Intellectual Property (2022)`. Naming, attribution, and integrity are perpetual and cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 433, text := "" },
  { number := 434, text := "#### 4.15.2 Attribution that survives assignment" },
  { number := 435, text := "" },
  { number := 436, text := "The statute keeps the moral right of attribution after assignment of copyright, or states that the right cannot be assigned during the Author's life. The pinned text does not contain a sentence that a waiver is void. The Contribution is still refused, because the Unlicense is not shown to extinguish attribution." },
  { number := 437, text := "" },
  { number := 438, text := "59. Albania. `Law 7564` Arts. 17 to 21. Perpetual moral rights; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 439, text := "60. Armenia. `Law of 2006` Art. 12. Unlimited moral rights; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 440, text := "61. Azerbaijan. `Law of 1996` Arts. 14 and 27. Unlimited moral rights; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 441, text := "62. Belarus. `Copyright Law` Art. 15. Unlimited moral rights; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 442, text := "63. Bulgaria. `Authors Rights and Related Rights Act` Art. 17 with Arts. 27 to 30. Attribution excepted from the ordinary term; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 443, text := "64. Ghana. `Copyright Act 2005` ss.6, 9, 18. A transfer of copyright does not include moral rights; moral rights are perpetual; no clause that a waiver is void is pinned." },
  { number := 444, text := "65. India. `Copyright Act 1957` s.57. Special rights survive assignment and, after 2012, survive expiry of copyright; not an article that a waiver is void." },
  { number := 445, text := "66. Kenya. `Copyright Act` s.32. Not transmissible during the Author's life." },
  { number := 446, text := "67. Latvia. `Copyright Law`. Cannot be transferred during the Author's life; article that a waiver is void is not pinned." },
  { number := 447, text := "68. Lithuania. `Law on Copyright` Art. 38(4) and Art. 34. Cannot be transferred; protected in perpetuity." },
  { number := 448, text := "69. Malta. `Copyright Act Cap. 415` s.12. Not transmissible during life; integrity requires consent." },
  { number := 449, text := "70. Nigeria. `Copyright Act 2022` s.14(3). Not transmissible during the Author's life." },
  { number := 450, text := "71. North Macedonia. `Author's Right Act 2010` Arts. 61(2) and 75. Unlimited moral rights; waiver clause not pinned." },
  { number := 451, text := "72. Qatar. `Law 7 of 2002` Arts. 10 to 11. Moral rights cannot expire by time and are perpetual." },
  { number := 452, text := "73. Republic of Korea. `Copyright Act` Art. 14. Moral rights belong exclusively to the Author." },
  { number := 453, text := "74. Switzerland. `Urheberrechtsgesetz` Arts. 9 and 11. Authorship and integrity recognized; no United Kingdom style waiver clause pinned." },
  { number := 454, text := "75. Taiwan. `Copyright Act` Arts. 21, 25, 26. Perpetual attribution; survives after economic rights end. Not a United Nations member." },
  { number := 455, text := "76. Uganda. `Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act` s.9(3). Not assignable except for enforcement." },
  { number := 456, text := "77. Ukraine. `Law 2811-IX`. Moral rights vest in the Author and cannot be transferred; ICLG 2026 states they cannot be waived." },
  { number := 457, text := "78. Slovenia. `Copyright and Related Rights Act` Articles 70(1) and 79. Moral rights may not be assigned; a contract transferring moral rights is null." },
  { number := 458, text := "79. Georgia. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 17(4). Alienation of personal non property rights during life is inadmissible." },
  { number := 459, text := "80. Kuwait. `Law 75/2019` Article 6. Moral rights are inalienable and not subject to assignment or attachment; any act relating to them is void." },
  { number := 460, text := "81. Costa Rica. `Ley 6683` Article 13. Moral right is personal, inalienable, cannot be given up, and perpetual." },
  { number := 461, text := "82. Uruguay. `Ley 9.739` Articles 12 and 13. Whatever the assignment contract says, the author keeps listed faculties over the work; withdrawal is personal and cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 462, text := "83. Morocco. `Law 2-00` Articles 9, 25, and 39. Moral rights cannot expire by time and are inalienable; cannot be transferred during life." },
  { number := 463, text := "84. Pakistan. `Copyright Ordinance` section 62. Author's special rights survive assignment and relinquishment of copyright." },
  { number := 464, text := "85. Tunisia. `Law 94-36` Article 8. Moral rights cannot expire by time, cannot be the object of a waiver, and are inalienable." },
  { number := 465, text := "86. Serbia. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Articles 14, 15, and 60. Paternity and attribution inalienable; cannot be waived or alienated by contract." },
  { number := 466, text := "87. Honduras. `Decreto 4-99-E` Article 35. Moral right personal, inalienable, cannot be given up, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 467, text := "88. Panama. `Law 15 of 1994` Article 29. Moral rights inalienable, cannot be attached, cannot be given up, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 468, text := "89. Paraguay. `Law 1.328/98` Article 17. Moral rights perpetual, inalienable, cannot be attached, cannot be given up, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 469, text := "90. Dominican Republic. `Law 65-00` Article 17. Perpetual, inalienable, cannot expire by time, and cannot be given up, including paternity." },
  { number := 470, text := "91. Venezuela. `Ley sobre el Derecho de Autor` Article 5. Moral rights inalienable, cannot be attached, cannot be given up." },
  { number := 471, text := "92. Iran. `1970 Copyright Law` Article 4. Intellectual rights have no place or time limit and cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 472, text := "93. Thailand. `Copyright Act B.E. 2537` section 18. The author is entitled to identify himself as author even against the assignee. The written agreement clause governs heir enforcement after death, not a living author's waiver." },
  { number := 473, text := "94. Lebanon. `Law 75/1999`. Moral rights perpetual, inalienable, and cannot expire by time. Article 53: moral rights enjoy perpetual protection not subject to prescription." },
  { number := 474, text := "95. El Salvador. `Decreto 66/2024` Article 10. Moral right cannot expire by time, inalienable, cannot be attached, and cannot be given up." },
  { number := 475, text := "96. Guatemala. `Ley de Derecho de Autor` Article 19. Inalienable, cannot expire by time, and cannot be given up." },
  { number := 476, text := "97. Mauritius. `Copyright Act 2014` section 7(3). Moral right cannot be assigned." },
  { number := 477, text := "98. Nauru. `Copyright Act 2019` section 13(3). Moral rights not capable of being assigned." },
  { number := 478, text := "99. Nicaragua. `Ley 312` Article 20. Moral rights cannot be given up and are inalienable." },
  { number := 479, text := "100. Bahrain. `Law 22/2006` Article 5. Eternal inalienable intangible rights including attribution. Alienation of any literary right is invalid." },
  { number := 480, text := "101. Bosnia and Herzegovina. `2010 Law` Article 31. Moral rights inalienable and not transmissible, including recognition as creator." },
  { number := 481, text := "102. Cambodia. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights 2003` Article 19. Moral right perpetual, inalienable, cannot be seized, cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 482, text := "103. Malawi. `Copyright Act 2016` section 30(4)(b). Moral rights may not be waived except for a use limited in nature and extent." },
  { number := 483, text := "104. Uzbekistan. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 17. Any agreement or statement in which the author renounces the exercise of moral rights is null and void." },
  { number := 484, text := "105. Lesotho. `Copyright Order 1989` section 8(2). Moral rights shall not be transferred." },
  { number := 485, text := "106. Rwanda. `Law 31/2009` Articles 216 and 228. Moral rights cannot expire by time and are inalienable; not transmissible during the author's life." },
  { number := 486, text := "107. Lao People's Democratic Republic. `Intellectual Property Law` Articles 100 and 101. Moral rights remain with the author and cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 487, text := "108. Namibia. `Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Protection Act 6 of 1994` section 25. The right to claim authorship survives transfer of copyright. No waiver article in the Act in force." },
  { number := 488, text := "109. Croatia. `Copyright and Related Rights Act` Article 64. The author cannot renounce his copyright. Article 56: copyright cannot be transferred except by inheritance. Article 15 written declaration only opts out of name indication for a particular use." },
  { number := 489, text := "110. Mongolia. `Law on Copyright` Article 12.1.3. The author may require his name to be mentioned whenever the work is published or exploited. Article 14.2: moral rights have no time limitation. Article 15.4: moral rights shall not be inherited." },
  { number := 490, text := "111. Kyrgyzstan. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 15(3). Moral rights are independent of property rights and are retained after assignment of the exclusive rights to use the work." },
  { number := 491, text := "112. Tajikistan. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 15. Moral rights belong to the author independently of economic rights and are retained after assignment of the exclusive right to exploit the work." },
  { number := 492, text := "113. Nepal. `Copyright Act 2059 (2002)` section 8(2). Moral rights shall not be transferable during the life of the author." },
  { number := 493, text := "114. Cuba. `Ley 154/2022` Article 17. Moral faculties include the right to recognition of authorship. Article 35.1 permits express waiver of economic faculties only." },
  { number := 494, text := "115. Zambia. `Copyright and Performance Rights Act Chapter 406` section 24. The right to be identified as author survives transfer of copyright and expires on the death of the author. No waiver article." },
  { number := 495, text := "116. Haiti. `Decree of 9 January 1968` Article 5. Moral extra patrimonial right inalienable and cannot be seized." },
  { number := 496, text := "117. Mozambique. `Lei 4/2001`. Moral rights inalienable, cannot be given up, cannot expire by time. `Lei 9/2022` Article 8: the right to claim authorship at any time after transfer of economic rights." },
  { number := 497, text := "118. Madagascar. Copyright statute Article 22. Moral rights perpetual, inalienable, cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 498, text := "119. Yemen. `Law 15/2012` Article 7. Moral rights eternal, cannot be assigned, not subject to disposition." },
  { number := 499, text := "120. Cyprus. `Law 59/1976` Article 7(4). During the author's life the author has the right to claim paternity of the work and to object to alteration. No waiver article in the Act as amended." },
  { number := 500, text := "121. Montenegro. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 71. The author may not assign moral rights. Article 80: a contract assigning moral rights is null and void." },
  { number := 501, text := "122. Jordan. `Copyright Protection Law No. 22 of 1992` Article 8(a). The author has the exclusive right to have the work attributed to him. Article 13: only economic rights may be transferred in writing." },
  { number := 502, text := "123. Liechtenstein. `Urheberrechtsgesetz` Article 9. The author has the exclusive right in the work and the right to recognition of authorship. No written waiver article." },
  { number := 503, text := "124. Syrian Arab Republic. `Legislative Decree 62 of 2013`. Moral rights of the author are perpetual and are not subject to limitation or disposal." },
  { number := 504, text := "125. Liberia. `Copyright Law` section 2.7(d). The moral rights of attribution and integrity shall not be transmissible during the life of the author." },
  { number := 505, text := "126. San Marino. `Law 8 of 25 January 1991` Article 27. The moral right of the author is personal, perpetual, inalienable, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 506, text := "127. Afghanistan. `Copyright Law 2008` Article 11(1). Moral rights of the work are confined to the author and cannot be transferred. Article 11(2) includes mention or no mention of name." },
  { number := 507, text := "128. Burundi. `Law No. 1/021 of 30 December 2005` Article 22. Moral rights attach to the author's person; perpetual, inalienable, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 508, text := "129. Ethiopia. `Copyright and Neighboring Rights Protection Proclamation 410/2004`. Moral rights exist irrespective of economic ownership and cannot be transferred during the author's life." },
  { number := 509, text := "130. Myanmar. `Copyright Law 2019` sections 18 to 21. Moral rights remain even if economic rights are transferred and cannot be transferred." },
  { number := 510, text := "131. United Republic of Tanzania. `Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act Cap. 218` section 11. The author has the right to claim authorship and to have authorship indicated. No waiver article in the Act." },
  { number := 511, text := "132. Iraq. `Law No. 3 of 1971` Article 8. Right of paternity perpetual, inalienable, cannot expire by time. Article 40: any disposal by a person other than the author of the rights in Articles 7, 8 and 10 is null." },
  { number := 512, text := "133. Bangladesh. `Copyright Act 2000` section 78. Author's special rights of attribution and integrity. The Act contains no waiver article." },
  { number := 513, text := "134. Democratic Republic of the Congo. `Ordonnance-loi n. 86-033 of 5 April 1986` Article 22. Moral rights attached to the person of the author; perpetual, cannot expire by time, and inalienable." },
  { number := 514, text := "135. Cabo Verde. `Decreto-legislativo n. 1/2009` Article 39. Moral rights inalienable, cannot be given up, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 515, text := "136. Monaco. `Loi n. 491 of 24 November 1948` Articles 19 and 20. The right of paternity is attached to the person of the author; perpetual and inalienable; its exercise cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 516, text := "137. Timor-Leste. `Codigo do Direito de Autor` Article 32. Moral rights inalienable, cannot be given up, and cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 517, text := "138. Libya. `Law No. 9 of 1968` Article 9. The author has the exclusive right to have the work attributed to him. No waiver article in the Act." },
  { number := 518, text := "139. Argentina. `Ley 11.723` Article 52. Although the author alienates the property of the work, he retains the right to demand fidelity of the text and title and the mention of his name or pseudonym as author." },
  { number := 519, text := "140. Sudan. `Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Protection Act 1996` section 8(1). Moral rights include attribution. Section 15(2) permits transfer of moral rights only if written, signed, and registered with period, place, and remuneration specified. The Unlicense is not that instrument." },
  { number := 520, text := "141. Democratic People's Republic of Korea. `Copyright Law` Article 20. The author's personal rights are not transferred nor inherited and have an unlimited period." },
  { number := 521, text := "142. Djibouti. `Law 154/AN/06` Article 9(5). Moral rights perpetual, inalienable, cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 522, text := "143. Sao Tome and Principe. `Codigo do Direito de Autor` Article 56(2). Moral rights inalienable, may not be waived, cannot expire by time." },
  { number := 523, text := "144. Suriname. `Auteurswet 1913` Article 25. Even after transfer of copyright the maker retains personality rights, including the right to oppose publication of the work under a name other than the maker's and the right to oppose a change in the designation of the maker." },
  { number := 524, text := "145. South Sudan. Constitution Article 198 keeps existing laws in force. The `Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Protection Act 1996` of Sudan remains the statute applied. Section 8(1) includes the right to claim authorship. Section 15(2) permits transfer of moral rights only if written, signed, and registered. The Unlicense is not that instrument." },
  { number := 525, text := "146. Turkmenistan. `Law No. 257-IV of 10 January 2012` Article 15(2). Personal non property rights, including the right of authorship and the right to a name, belong to the author independently of property rights and remain after assignment of the exclusive rights to use the work." },
  { number := 526, text := "147. Somalia. `Law No. 66 of 7 September 1977` Article 15(3) and 15(4). Moral rights of attribution and integrity subsist after transfer of economic rights and are inalienable and cannot be assigned." },
  { number := 527, text := "148. Eritrea. `Transitional Civil Code` Article 1665. Notwithstanding any stipulation to the contrary, the author may prevent his work, if altered by a third party, from being presented as his own. Article 1671: that right may be exercised after death by the author's spouse, ascendants, children, and grandchildren." },
  { number := 528, text := "150. Holy See. `Law CXXXII of 19 March 2011` Article 1, as continued by `Law CXCVII of 1 September 2017`. Unless otherwise provided, Vatican City observes Italian copyright legislation. Italy `Legge 22 aprile 1941 n. 633` Articles 20 to 22: the right of paternity is inalienable and cannot be waived." },
  { number := 529, text := "151. Kosovo. `Law No. 08/L-205 on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 19(1). Independently of economic rights and even after assignment the author has the right to claim authorship. Article 22(1): moral rights shall not be transferable by assignment or license." },
  { number := 530, text := "152. State of Palestine. No successor waiver statute opened. West Bank practice applies Jordan `Copyright Protection Law No. 22 of 1992` Article 8(a). Gaza historically applied Egyptian `Law No. 354 of 1954`. Jordan and Egypt are already on the Residual attribution list." },
  { number := 531, text := "153. Somaliland. Somalia `Law No. 66 of 7 September 1977` Article 15(3) and 15(4), treated as the copyright statute in Somaliland (`somalilandlaw.com`). Moral rights of attribution and integrity subsist after transfer of economic rights and are inalienable and cannot be assigned." },
  { number := 532, text := "154. Abkhazia. `Law No. 1227-c-XIV on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 15(3). Personal non property rights belong to the author independently of property rights and are retained after assignment of exclusive rights of use." },
  { number := 533, text := "155. South Ossetia. `Law on Copyright and Related Rights` Article 15(3). Personal non property rights belong to the author independently of property rights and are retained after assignment of exclusive rights of use. `parliamentrso.org`." },
  { number := 534, text := "156. Transnistria. `Civil Code of the Pridnestrovian Moldavian Republic` Article 1292. The author has the right of authorship and the author's right to a name. Official commentary: the right of authorship, the right to a name, and the right to protect reputation are perpetual." },
  { number := 535, text := "" },
  { number := 536, text := "The numbering skips 149 because the source list has no item 149. The named count is 155 jurisdictions (146 United Nations members plus Macao, Taiwan, the Holy See, Kosovo, the State of Palestine, Somaliland, Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Transnistria)." },
  { number := 537, text := "" },
  { number := 538, text := "### 4.16 Unread list" },
  { number := 539, text := "" },
  { number := 540, text := "The copyright statute of each jurisdiction on the Unread list has not been classified into Clause 4.13, Clause 4.14, or Clause 4.15. Nationals of those jurisdictions SHALL NOT contribute until the statute is read and the jurisdiction is placed on the Allow list. Unread is not a finding either way. Unread is refusal until classification." },
  { number := 541, text := "" },
  { number := 542, text := "1. United Nations members not classified in Clause 4.13, Clause 4.14, or Clause 4.15: 0 United Nations members. Every United Nations member is named in those clauses." },
  { number := 543, text := "2. Non member jurisdictions and observers not classified in those clauses: 0 jurisdictions. Every named non member and de facto jurisdiction in this specification is in those clauses, or is closed under the parent state rule in item 3 of this clause." },
  { number := 544, text := "3. A Contributor who is a national of the parent state is classified under that parent state:" },
  { number := 545, text := "	1. Faroe Islands and Greenland follow Denmark." },
  { number := 546, text := "	2. Aland follows Finland." },
  { number := 547, text := "	3. Svalbard follows Norway." },
  { number := 548, text := "	4. French overseas collectivities follow France." },
  { number := 549, text := "	5. Puerto Rico and other United States territories follow the United States, for persons who are United States nationals." },
  { number := 550, text := "	6. Crown Dependencies and British Overseas Territories follow the United Kingdom, for persons who are British citizens. Jersey, Guernsey, and the Isle of Man also have their own statutes of waiver in writing and are named on the Allow list." },
  { number := 551, text := "	7. Tokelau follows New Zealand. The people of Tokelau are New Zealand citizens." },
  { number := 552, text := "4. A person who holds only a local status that is not citizenship of an Allow list state is unread." },
  { number := 553, text := "5. Stating that unread United Nations members remaining is none is a classification claim, not a statute pin." },
  { number := 554, text := "" },
  { number := 555, text := "### 4.17 Attestation" },
  { number := 556, text := "" },
  { number := 557, text := "The Contributor SHALL state, in writing with the Contribution:" },
  { number := 558, text := "" },
  { number := 559, text := "1. each nationality they hold;" },
  { number := 560, text := "2. that every such nationality is on the Allow list;" },
  { number := 561, text := "3. that they dedicate the Contribution under the Unlicense." },
  { number := 562, text := "" },
  { number := 563, text := "No passport, national identity card, or copyright registration is requested or accepted as a condition of contribution." },
  { number := 564, text := "" },
  { number := 565, text := "### 4.18 Request to re-read a statute" },
  { number := 566, text := "" },
  { number := 567, text := "A national of a jurisdiction named on any list in this specification who wants a statute re-read, or who wants a classification clarified, MAY write to `legal@surmount.systems`." },
  { number := 568, text := "" },
  { number := 569, text := "`legal@surmount.systems` is not a private mailbox. Mail sent to that address is published on the Surmount website. It is not a confidential communication and MUST NOT be treated as one. Authors SHALL NOT send passports, national identity cards, copyright registrations, or other government identity documents to that address." },
  { number := 570, text := "" },
  { number := 571, text := "### 4.19 Informative figure (contributor nationality map)" },
  { number := 572, text := "" },
  { number := 573, text := "This subsection is informative. Numbered specifications SHALL NOT embed binary image assets. This ASCII markdown cannot embed SVG. The file [contributor-nationality-map.svg](contributor-nationality-map.svg) is a supporting figure at this repository root. It is not a numbered specification. Geometry is Natural Earth 1:110m public domain. Classification colors follow this specification. The map is not the Allow list. Normative lists remain the numbered lists in Clause 4.13, Clause 4.14, Clause 4.15, and Clause 4.16." },
  { number := 574, text := "" },
  { number := 575, text := "### 4.20 Counts and scale (informative)" },
  { number := 576, text := "" },
  { number := 577, text := "This subsection is informative. Figures of population and GDP are scale, not a legal test. A Contribution is accepted or refused by nationality and statute, not by these totals." },
  { number := 578, text := "" },
  { number := 579, text := "| List | Effect on contribution | Named jurisdictions |" },
  { number := 580, text := "|---|---|---|" },
  { number := 581, text := "| Allow | accepted with the Unlicense | 54 |" },
  { number := 582, text := "| Specific consent | refused on the Unlicense alone | 2 |" },
  { number := 583, text := "| Residual attribution | refused | 155 (146 United Nations members plus Macao, Taiwan, the Holy See, Kosovo, the State of Palestine, Somaliland, Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Transnistria) |" },
  { number := 584, text := "| Unread United Nations members | refused until classified onto Allow | 0 |" },
  { number := 585, text := "| Unread other jurisdictions | refused until classified onto Allow | 0 |" },
  { number := 586, text := "" },
  { number := 587, text := "193 United Nations members equal 45 Allow plus 2 specific consent plus 146 residual attribution plus 0 unread." },
  { number := 588, text := "" },
  { number := 589, text := "| List | Population (UN WPP 2024 mid 2026) | Share of UN WPP world | GDP (IMF WEO April 2026) | Share of IMF world GDP |" },
  { number := 590, text := "|---|---|---|---|---|" },
  { number := 591, text := "| Allow (United Nations members plus Hong Kong SAR) | about 773 million | 9.4% | about $44.1 trillion | 34.9% |" },
  { number := 592, text := "| Specific consent | about 62 million | 0.8% | about $2.43 trillion | 1.9% |" },
  { number := 593, text := "| Residual attribution (remainder) | about 7.40 billion | 89.8% | about $79.7 trillion | 63.1% |" },
  { number := 594, text := "| World | 8.23 billion (UN) / 8.05 billion (IMF pop) | 100% | $126.30 trillion | 100% |" },
  { number := 595, text := "" },
  { number := 596, text := "Allow is small in population and large in GDP because the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, the Netherlands, Ireland, and Singapore sit on Allow. Residual attribution is most of the world's people, including China and India. Sources: United Nations World Population Prospects 2024; International Monetary Fund World Economic Outlook, April 2026. Those sources are not Clause 12 pins." },
  { number := 597, text := "" },
  { number := 598, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 599, text := "" },
  { number := 600, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 601, text := "" },
  { number := 602, text := "1. Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is treated as the ideal, and the PDOSS test is the public domain dedication of software that is open (Clause 3.4, Clause 3.5, and Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 603, text := "2. Unlicense remains the license; the most important Surmount work in this repository is dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense; companion Lean treats an Unlicense dedication as having no remaining copyright in the model and as meeting the PDOSS test (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 604, text := "3. MIT as used by the Lean 4 agent skill pack does not meet a public domain dedication test and does not meet the PDOSS test; Apache 2.0 as used by the `btc-verified` pin does not meet a public domain dedication test and does not meet the PDOSS test; a mash that claims MIT meets PDOSS is `False` (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 605, text := "4. A grant that keeps copyright is treated as still leaving a copyright holder, and remaining copyright is treated as still letting a later contract take the work (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 606, text := "5. Ideas are treated as not scarce; two people can hold the same idea at once; generosity of ideas is the default this repository chooses (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 607, text := "6. Numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree are released under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license; the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT; the `btc-verified` pin remains Apache 2.0; essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 608, text := "7. Refusing a tool the author cannot improve is treated as RSI process residual and is not treated as a claim that every product is Unlicense (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 609, text := "8. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true; proofs live in separate Lean modules; a mash that hides the split is treated as `False`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 610, text := "9. Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URL; a numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags also contains the host `proofofkeags.com`; theorems cover exactly what they state (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 611, text := "10. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, Continuous Integration, Lean Machine, and Majestic Memex are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 612, text := "11. fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; number 0009 is this specification and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist; the Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 does not exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 613, text := "12. The named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.11)." },
  { number := 614, text := "13. A Contribution is accepted only if it is dedicated under the Unlicense and every nationality the Contributor holds is on the Allow list; a Contribution is refused if any nationality is on the Residual attribution list, the Specific consent list, or the Unread list; dual or multiple nationality refuses if any one citizenship is not Allow; Users of a published Work are not restricted by nationality; companion Lean treats a mash that a residual attribution national Contribution is accepted as `False` (Clause 4.12 through Clause 4.16)." },
  { number := 615, text := "" },
  { number := 616, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming Surmount product. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 617, text := "" },
  { number := 618, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to." },
  { number := 619, text := "" },
  { number := 620, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 621, text := "" },
  { number := 622, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 623, text := "" },
  { number := 624, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 625, text := "" },
  { number := 626, text := "1. fargo is not specified. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, or 0011 for fargo. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 627, text := "2. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 628, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is this specification. Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 629, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 630, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if either of those files is present. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept." },
  { number := 631, text := "" },
  { number := 632, text := "### 6.2 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 633, text := "" },
  { number := 634, text := "1. This document specifies Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) and records that Unlicense remains the license. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 635, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds. The match is not claimed done. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use." },
  { number := 636, text := "3. `lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean` proves those claims. `lean/Surmount.lean` composes stack identities including this specification as number 0009. `0009_PDOSS.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0009.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that Slake emit already matches `ELF`. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use. They are not a proof that every file in a clone is Unlicense." },
  { number := 637, text := "" },
  { number := 638, text := "### 6.3 Named residual licenses this Unlicense does not replace" },
  { number := 639, text := "" },
  { number := 640, text := "1. The Lean 4 agent skill pack at `skills/lean4-skills` is original work under the MIT license. It is not under `ref/`. It is not a Clause 12 pin. It is not `mathlib`. This repository's Unlicense does not replace that MIT license. MIT does not meet the PDOSS test." },
  { number := 641, text := "2. The `btc-verified` pin at `ref/btc-verified` is Apache 2.0. This repository's Unlicense does not replace that Apache 2.0 license. Apache 2.0 does not meet the PDOSS test." },
  { number := 642, text := "3. Essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. They are not Unlicense grants. Local copies under `ref/philosophy/proofofkeags/` are for readers. They are not a public domain grant of those essays. `ref/philosophy/proofofkeags/SOURCE.md` records that back linking is ideal, that the jurisdiction he named is USA, and that the Unlicense of this repository does not apply the Unlicense to those essays. Full license text is still not published on https://proofofkeags.com . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 643, text := "4. Product trees outside this repository MAY name a different license in their own residual. This document does not claim those trees are Unlicense." },
  { number := 644, text := "" },
  { number := 645, text := "### 6.4 Pins this document does not add" },
  { number := 646, text := "" },
  { number := 647, text := "1. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`. `0002_Systems_Lean.md` places those Form 1 pins in the Systems Lean product tree. This repository MUST NOT copy those four trees into this repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 648, text := "2. https://unlicense.org is informative prior art. It is not a Clause 12 pin. This repository does not add a Form 1 or Form 2 pin of that site. The binding dedication is `UNLICENSE.md`." },
  { number := 649, text := "3. ISO 24495-1:2023 and the US Federal Plain Language Guidelines remain informative prior art of CATE. They are not pins of this document." },
  { number := 650, text := "4. Other public domain instruments (for example CC0) are not pinned here. Companion Lean MUST NOT encode CC0 as meeting the PDOSS test. This document does not claim CC0 fails or meets PDOSS as a pinned instrument. CC0 remains residual." },
  { number := 651, text := "" },
  { number := 652, text := "### 6.5 Informative items this document names" },
  { number := 653, text := "" },
  { number := 654, text := "1. Formal Vibefication research pages in Clause 2.2 are not Clause 12 pins of this document." },
  { number := 655, text := "2. CATE is specified in `0005_CATE.md`. CATE is not this specification." },
  { number := 656, text := "3. RSI is specified in `0006_RSI.md`. RSI is not this specification." },
  { number := 657, text := "4. Formal Vibefication is specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Formal Vibefication is not this specification." },
  { number := 658, text := "5. Surmount Systems is specified in `0010_Surmount_Systems.md`. Surmount Systems is not this specification." },
  { number := 659, text := "6. Companion models for CATE (`lean/CateSpec.lean` encodings, `lean/CateProofs.lean` theorems), RSI (`lean/RsiSpec.lean`, `lean/RsiProofs.lean`), Continuous Integration (`lean/CiSpec.lean`, `lean/CiProofs.lean`), beastdb (encodings and proofs under `lean/` for that product), SSSSS (`lean/SssssSpec.lean`, `lean/SssssProofs.lean`), Systems Lean (`lean/SystemsLeanSpec.lean`, `lean/SystemsLeanProofs.lean`), Formal Vibefication (`lean/FormalVibeficationSpec.lean`, `lean/FormalVibeficationProofs.lean`), PDOSS (`lean/UnlicenseSpec.lean`, `lean/UnlicenseProofs.lean`), Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`lean/TechTreeSpec.lean`, `lean/TechTreeProofs.lean`), Majestic Memex (`lean/MemexSpec.lean`, `lean/MemexProofs.lean`), Lean Machine (`lean/LeanMachineSpec.lean`, `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`), and the CATE word catalog (`lean/VocabularySpec.lean`, `lean/VocabularyProofs.lean`) place encodings in Spec modules and theorems in Proofs modules. Collision tags in `lean/Vocabulary.lean` are encodings with proofs in `lean/VocabularyCollisionProofs.lean`. Mixing those in one mash is `False` under `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. Sibling line encodings remain a separate split." },
  { number := 660, text := "" },
  { number := 661, text := "### 6.6 Contributor nationality residual" },
  { number := 662, text := "" },
  { number := 663, text := "1. Stating that unread United Nations members remaining is none, and that unread other jurisdictions remaining is none, is a classification claim. It is not a statute pin. Unread remains refusal until classification. A later re-read MAY move a jurisdiction." },
  { number := 664, text := "2. Population and GDP tables in Clause 4.20 are scale, not the legal test. A Contribution is accepted or refused by nationality and statute, not by those totals. United Nations World Population Prospects 2024 and IMF World Economic Outlook April 2026 are not Clause 12 pins of this document." },
  { number := 665, text := "3. The file `contributor-nationality-map.svg` is an informative figure. Geometry is Natural Earth 1:110m public domain. The map is not the Allow list. Normative lists remain the numbered lists in this specification." },
  { number := 666, text := "4. Statute cites in Clause 4.13, Clause 4.14, and Clause 4.15 are not Clause 12 `ref/` pins unless the operator pins them. This document does not add those statutes under `ref/`." },
  { number := 667, text := "5. The contributor nationality condition is inbound only. Users of a published Work are not restricted by nationality. Dual or multiple nationality refuses if any one citizenship is not on the Allow list. That refuse is any not Allow class, not a separate license." },
  { number := 668, text := "6. Unlicense remains the license. The Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 MUST NOT exist." },
  { number := 669, text := "" },
  { number := 670, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 671, text := "" },
  { number := 672, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260920" },
  { number := 673, text := "" },
  { number := 674, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS). The file name is `0009_PDOSS.md`. Unlicense remains the license. Defines the PDOSS test. Records that Unlicense meets that test. Records that MIT as used by the Lean 4 agent skill pack and Apache 2.0 as used by the `btc-verified` pin do not meet a public domain dedication test. Records that a mash that claims MIT meets PDOSS is `False`. Records the contributor nationality agreement: a Contribution is accepted only if dedicated under the Unlicense and every nationality is on the Allow list; Specific consent, Residual attribution, and Unread refuse; dual nationality refuses if any one citizenship is not Allow; Users of a published Work are not restricted by nationality. Residual records that other public domain instruments (for example CC0) are not pinned here, that unread remaining none is a classification claim, that GDP and population tables are scale, that the Natural Earth map is informative, and that statute cites are not Clause 12 pins. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed for Unlicense as numbered specification 0009, and that number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now PDOSS." },
  { number := 675, text := "" },
  { number := 676, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260826" },
  { number := 677, text := "" },
  { number := 678, text := "First publication of Unlicense as numbered specification 0009. The operator assigned 0009 to fill the gap after Vocabulary was folded into CATE. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then withdrawn; it was then Unlicense by operator order. A numbered Vocabulary file remains forbidden. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Records that a grant that keeps copyright still lets a later contract take the work. Requires the most important Surmount work in this repository (numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree) to be dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense so it stays the common heritage of anyone who seeks it, outside a later private claim. Records that ideas are not scarce and that two people can hold the same idea at once. Requires authors to release numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license. Records that the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT and that essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense. Records that refusing a tool the author cannot improve is RSI process residual and is not a claim that every product is Unlicense. Records Formal Vibefication as the split that encodes this specification in Lean and keeps proofs in separate modules, with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Treats a mash of spec encodings and their proofs that hides the split as nonconforming. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use." },
  { number := 679, text := "" },
  { number := 680, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Formal Vibefication is specification 0008; Surmount Systems is specification 0010; this specification is number 0009; the word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`); a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP is not specified; Carbonado has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; honesty notes for Proof of Keags copies live at `ref/philosophy/proofofkeags/SOURCE.md`; this document does not claim that a conforming Surmount product exists." },
  { number := 681, text := "" },
